# ==============================================================================
# SSH Local Configuration Overrides (~/.ssh/config.override)
# ==============================================================================
#
# This file is for local, machine-specific overrides and additions to your
# SSH configuration. Chezmoi creates this file once as a template and will
# NEVER overwrite your local edits here.
#
# Evaluation Order:
#   1. Specific host configurations in ~/.ssh/config.d/*.conf
#   2. This file (~/.ssh/config.override)
#   3. Global defaults in ~/.ssh/config (Host *)
#
# Because OpenSSH uses first-match-wins per directive:
#   - Directives defined here take precedence over global defaults in ~/.ssh/config.
#   - Specific host definitions in ~/.ssh/config.d/ take precedence over this file.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Examples:
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Override or set a default username across all hosts:
# Host *
#   User myuser
#   ConnectTimeout 5
#
# Custom work bastion / jump host:
# Host internal-*
#   ProxyJump jumpuser@bastion.example.com
#
# Hostname canonicalization (auto-expand short names with search domains):
# CanonicalDomains accepts multiple whitespace-separated domain suffixes.
# Host *
#   CanonicalizeHostname yes
#   CanonicalDomains corp.example.com lab.example.com
#   CanonicalizeFallbackLocal yes
